%% Tool Scoping — two code branches, dynamic overrides per phase
%% Why "advance" appears and disappears between protocol phases.
%% The tool list mutates at runtime and is re-pushed over MCP.

sequenceDiagram
    participant daemon as daemon.ts
    participant runner as protocol-<br/>runner.ts
    participant tools as bridge-<br/>tools.ts
    participant transport as bridge-<br/>transport.ts
    participant bridge as bridge.ts
    participant cc as Claude Code<br/>session

    Note over tools: computeToolsForSession has two branches:
    Note over tools: sessionId === 'main' → all UNIVERSAL_TOOLS<br/>everyone else → minus MASTER_ORCHESTRATOR_ONLY<br/>(spawn_session, kill_session) and minus<br/>PROTOCOL_ONLY (advance, extend_phase)<br/>unless scopedToolOverrides provided

    Note over daemon: On spawn / bridge registration
    daemon->>tools: computeToolsForSession(sessionId)
    tools->>tools: filter: main gets all,<br/>others lose fleet tools + protocol tools
    daemon->>transport: send tools in "registered" msg
    transport->>bridge: {type: registered, tools: [...]}
    bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed

    Note over runner: On protocol phase transition
    runner->>runner: refreshRunTools(run)
    loop for each participant
        runner->>runner: scopedToolOverridesForRun(sessionId)
        Note over runner: returns {advance: "phase-specific description"}<br/>only for the ACTIVE actor in this phase.<br/>Non-active actors get no overrides →<br/>advance filtered out by computeToolsForSession
        runner->>tools: computeToolsForSession(sid, {scopedToolOverrides})
        tools->>tools: include advance + extend_phase<br/>with override descriptions
        runner->>transport: {type: tools_update, tools: [...]}
        transport->>bridge: tools_update
        bridge->>bridge: dynamicTools = tools
        bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
    end

    Note over cc: Claude calls ListTools
    cc->>bridge: ListToolsRequest
    bridge->>cc: dynamicTools (current set)
    Note over cc: advance is present only during<br/>the session's active phase turn

    Note over tools: Codex sessions: STATIC tools.<br/>codex-mcp-server.ts computes once at<br/>startup with advance always included.<br/>No tools_update, no list_changed.
